doc.markdown:
Width counts **octets**; the fill is exactly **one literal octet** (a run fill raises; so does a rune whose
encoding is more than one octet). Default fill is the space octet. A width at or below the length is a no-op;
one past `4294967296` octets raises rather than exhausting the host.

doc.code:
d := d"2026-01-31"
d.components()              // => {"day": 31, "month": 1, "year": 2026}
date(d.components()) == d   // => true

1d / 3d                             // => 0.3333333333333333333d — 19 places, the rest dropped
decimal("0.0000000001") * decimal("0.0000000001")
                                    // 0.0000000000000000000d — the exact 1e-20 needs 20 places,
                                    // so it rounds to zero at scale 19

doc.markdown:
`pow(exponent)` takes an integer exponent and truncates at the 19-place ceiling as it goes, like the operators;
for a long compounding chain, `pow_round(k, n, mode)` carries guard digits and rounds once (see
[the `*_round` members](kavun:type/decimal#arithmetic-straight-to-a-scale--the-_round-members)):

doc.code:
io := import("io")

safe_div := func(a, b) res {
    defer func() {
        e := recover()
        if e != undefined {
            io.print("caught: ", e.kind())   // "division_by_zero"
            res = 0
        }
    }()
    res = a / b
}

safe_div(10, 2)   // => 5
safe_div(10, 0)   // prints "caught: division_by_zero", answers 0

defer func() {
    e := recover()
    if e == undefined {
        return                          // nothing in flight
    }
    if e.kind() == "division_by_zero" {
        // handle this one
    } else {
        raise(e)                        // not ours — let it keep unwinding
    }
}()

amount := 5d                          // the host's binding
require(amount > 0d, {field: "amount", reason: "must be positive"})
// host: re.Payload is that record, not a sentence to re-parse

io = import("io")

checked_add = func(a, b) res {
    defer func() {
        e = recover()
        if e != undefined { res = undefined; io.print("overflow: ", string(e)) }
    }()
    res = a + b
}

acc := []
for x in range(10, 0, 3) {
    acc = acc + x
}
// acc == [10, 7, 4, 1]

[2, 3] in range(1, 10)                    // Error: not_implemented — deferred (not_implemented)
(2..4) in range(1, 10)                    // Error: not_implemented — deferred
func(x) { return x > 2 } in range(1, 10)  // Error: invalid_value — write r.any(fn)

acc := []
range(5, 8).for_each(func(i, x) { acc = acc + [[i, x]] })
// acc == [[0, 5], [1, 6], [2, 7]]

r = {a: 1}
c = record(r)                    // a new record
c.a = 9                          // r.a is still 1

for k in {a: 1, b: 2} {}           // "a", "b" — the keys
for k, v in {a: 1, b: 2} {}        // ("a", 1), ("b", 2)
for _, v in {a: 1, b: 2} {}        // 1, 2 — the values spelling

doc.markdown:
An [octet escape](kavun:type/string#undecodable-octets) is spelled `'\udcNN'` (or `'\U0000DCNN'`), NN = `80`–`ff`;
every other surrogate is a parse error. `'\xff'` is `U+00FF` (`ÿ`), a symbol — not the escape. The `v` and `q`
renders write an escape in the same spelling, so a render always reads back as the rune it came from:

doc.code:
time({year: 2026, month: 3, day: 29, hour: 3, minute: 30, zone: "Europe/Kyiv"})
// Error: invalid_value: (time) 2026-03-29 03:30:00 does not exist in zone Europe/Kyiv (a daylight-saving gap)
time({year: 2026, month: 10, day: 25, hour: 3, minute: 30, zone: "Europe/Kyiv"})
// Error: invalid_value: (time) ... occurs twice in zone Europe/Kyiv (a daylight-saving overlap): give zone_offset to pick one
time({year: 2026, month: 10, day: 25, hour: 3, minute: 30, zone: "Europe/Kyiv", zone_offset: 7200})
// => time("2026-10-25T03:30:00+02:00") — the second 03:30

1 in undefined          // Error: invalid_binary_operator — membership in an
                        // absent container is a program error, not an absent answer
u := undefined
u()                     // Error: not_callable
for x in undefined { }  // Error: not_iterable — absence has no elements,
                        // not zero of them; is_iterable(undefined) is false
